<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muyeol of Silla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 661</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Kim Chunchu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muyeol, born Kim Chunchu, was king of Silla from 654 to 661, the first king from the 'true bone' rank. As a diplomat he secured an alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a> in 648, and as king he joined the Tang in destroying Baekje in 660, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kim-yu-sin">Kim Yu-sin</a> commanding the Silla army. His son Munmu completed the unification of most of the Korean peninsula.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muyeol-of-silla.jpg" alt="Muyeol of Silla" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christophe95 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portraits_of_kings_at_Tongiljeon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
